                  "text": "I'm working out the grid dimensions (10 rows by 9 columns, using identity orientation since portrait) and tracing diagonal paths for x5 and x7 to find where they intersect the grid boundaries.\n\nContinuing to build up the transformed shapes through unions and corner removals - checking llcorner and ulcorner positions, computing heights, and testing shift intervals against grid bounds to see which fall off-screen.\n\nNow I'm identifying which corner holds color 1 (it's the lower-left corner), then applying a horizontal mirror transformation to the diagonal shape - reflecting each cell across the row axis to get new coordinates I'll fill with 1s.\n\nSo the diagonal now runs from row0/col7 down to row9/col0, one cell per row, decreasing column as row increases.\n\n",
